    "long_instructions": "\r\n# Using the Backpack Feature\r\n\r\n#### The previous level instructed you to use the backpack feature.\r\n\r\n#### The backpack feature in coding platforms allows you to save and reuse code  across different projects.\r\n\r\n## How to Save to the Backpack\r\n\r\n#### Students should get in the habit of saving their files after each level they build in it. This way, they can easily access the code on future projects. \r\n\r\n- #### Click the three-dot menu icon next to the `index.html` file name.\r\n- #### Select \"Save to backpack\" from the drop-down menu.\r\n- #### Name the file and press save.\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/a5083c7ccc54bfa4ea561fa29adf2902-image-1740077664809.gif\" alt=\"gif of how to use the backpack\" width=\"650px\" style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\r\n\r\n\r\n## How to Import the Backpack \r\n#### Students can import their previous work to use on current projects. \r\n\r\n- #### Click the `+` icon next to the File menu.\r\n- #### Select \"Import from backpack\" from the drop-down menu.\r\n- #### Select your file and click the \"Import to project\" button.\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/f53f681651f42c532cf0c7078fc14099-image-1740078209718.gif\" alt=\"gif of how to use the backpack\" width=\"650px\" style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Step-by-Step Tutorial\r\n\r\n#### Not sure about the last level? Check out this quick tutorial for a step-by-step walk through.\r\n\r\n"
  },
